# What firstmate relies on no-mistakes to keep meaning.
#
# Consumer: bin/fm-crew-state.sh, which judges a validating crewmate by the run
# step reported by `no-mistakes axi status` rather than by pane liveness. If the
# axi surface were renamed, fm-crew-state.sh would fall through to the pane and
# silently downgrade to the exact stale-status reading the run-step read exists
# to replace.
#
# Deliberately NOT pinned: the version floor, which bin/fm-bootstrap.sh's
# no_mistakes_compatible already owns and reports as MISSING: no-mistakes - a
# second copy here would report the same fact twice. Also not pinned: the TOON
# field names inside a status document. They
# are read with tolerant greps rather than a strict parser, and pinning the full
# document would be maintenance against a surface firstmate reads loosely on
# purpose. The subcommand vocabulary is what a rename would break.

probe axi = no-mistakes axi --help

#: `axi status` is the run-step source of truth fm-crew-state.sh reads
text axi  status

#: `axi run` is the validation entrypoint the ship brief points crewmates at
text axi  run

#: `axi respond` is the gate-answer path firstmate routes captain decisions back through
text axi  respond
